## Requirements

* JDK 17 or newer on `PATH` (`java -version`)
* Android SDK for device/emulator installs (Android Studio installs it), with
  `ANDROID_HOME` set
* No Gradle install needed: `./gradlew` bootstraps Gradle {{ gradle_version }}

## Build

```sh
./gradlew assembleDebug      # -> app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
./gradlew test               # JVM unit tests
./gradlew installDebug       # install on a connected device/emulator
./gradlew clean
```

MakeMaker can drive these for you:

```sh
makemaker build .
makemaker test .
```

## Layout

```
{{ slug }}/
├── settings.gradle.kts
├── build.gradle.kts        plugin versions
├── gradle.properties
├── gradlew / gradlew.bat   bootstraps Gradle on first run
└── app/
    ├── build.gradle.kts
    ├── proguard-rules.pro
    └── src/
        ├── main/
        │   ├── AndroidManifest.xml
        │   ├── java/{{ package_path }}/
        │   │   ├── MainActivity.kt
        │   │   └── Greeter.kt      framework-free logic
        │   └── res/                layout, strings, theme, colours, icon
        └── test/java/{{ package_path }}/
            └── GreeterTest.kt      JUnit tests (./gradlew test)
```

## Notes

`Greeter.kt` holds the app's logic with no Android imports, so `./gradlew test`
runs it on the JVM in seconds -- no emulator required. Move real logic there as
the app grows.
